{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"391ddae3-05ce-488d-8baf-2d4370d2b0f6","step_index":26,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.344695,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"head -n 25 wayfinder/tickets/*.md"},"output":"==\u003e wayfinder/tickets/ticket-001.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 001: Entity Anchor Linking and Layperson Vocabulary Normalization Specification\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-001.md`  \r\n**Scope:** GraphRAG Stage 1 - Input Entity Resolution  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-graphrag-spec`  \r\n**Blocked By:** None (Root Decision)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow must the system deterministically resolve unstructured natural language inputs from real-world patients, clinicians, and researchers (e.g., *\"I am from Wisconsin, survived breast cancer, need lymphedema supplies, I'm on Medicare\"*) into precise graph entry points without probabilistic guessing or fragile hardcoded regex rules?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Decision and Specification Requirements\r\n\r\n### 2.1. Deterministic Multi-Slot Entity Resolution\r\nThe system must parse unstructured natural language into three orthogonal domain slots:\r\n1. **Geographic Entity Anchor (`State`):**\r\n   - Matches state names, state abbreviations, and territorial designations against the indexed `State` entities (`STATE-[state_code]`).\r\n   - Example: `\"Wisconsin\"` $\\rightarrow$ `STATE-WI`.\r\n2. **Clinical Indication Anchor (`ICD10Code`):**\r\n   - Maps clinical lay terms and medical histories to formal ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes using indexed lexical matching on `code` and `description`.\r\n   - Examples:\r\n\r\n==\u003e wayfinder/tickets/ticket-002.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 002: Generalized Topological Subgraph Expansion and Neighborhood Traversal Specification\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-002.md`  \r\n**Scope:** GraphRAG Stage 2 - Graph Topology Retrieval  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-graphrag-spec`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-001.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow must the graph retrieval engine traverse the knowledge graph between resolved anchors without generating bespoke Cypher queries for every anticipated user question, while strictly preserving system invariants (`INV-UNBROKEN-ANCESTRY`, `INV-NO-KEYWORD-BRIDGING`, and `INV-50-STATE-COMPLETENESS`)?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Decision and Specification Requirements\r\n\r\n### 2.1. Generalized $k$-Hop Connecting Subgraph Extraction\r\nRather than attempting to guess specialized Cypher queries, the system must execute a single, generalized topological path discovery algorithm:\r\n1. **Target Endpoints:** Identified anchors from Stage 1:\r\n   - Source: `{State: S, ICD10Code: D, Policy: P}`\r\n2. **Topological Join Contracts:**\r\n   The traversal engine extracts the intersection subgraph linking:\r\n   - **Contractor \u0026 Administrative Lineage:**\r\n     $$(S) \\longleftarrow [\\text{:COVERS\\_STATE}] - (J: \\text{Jurisdiction}) \\longleftarrow [\\text{:APPLIES\\_TO\\_JURISDICTION}] - (CR: \\text{ChangeRequest}) \\longrightarrow [\\text{:MANDATES\\_POLICY}] \\longrightarrow (CP: \\text{CoveragePolicy})$$\r\n\r\n==\u003e wayfinder/tickets/ticket-003.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 003: Factual Context Assembly, Edge Provenance Formatting, and Prompt Grounding Specification\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-003.md`  \r\n**Scope:** GraphRAG Stage 3 - Context Synthesis \u0026 Grounding  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-graphrag-spec`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-002.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow must the retrieved subgraph and its provenance metadata be transformed into prompt context for Hugging Face open-weight instruction models to ensure 100% grounded answers, zero hallucination of payment rates or legal rules, and clear citations to primary sources?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Decision and Specification Requirements\r\n\r\n### 2.1. Deterministic Factual Serialization Format\r\nThe retrieved nodes and relationships must be formatted into clean, structured Markdown/triple statements before injection into the prompt:\r\n1. **Administrative Authority Block:**\r\n   ```markdown\r\n   - Program Authority: Medicare Part B DMEPOS\r\n   - Authorizing Policy Article: [CMS-MCD-A59508] \"Standard Documentation Requirements for Lymphedema Compression Treatment Items\"\r\n   - Operational Transmittal: [CMS-CR-13286] Transmittal 12349\r\n   - Regional Claims Contractor: [JURIS-DME-B] CGS Administrators (Covers: Wisconsin, Illinois, Indiana, Kentucky, Michigan, Minnesota, Ohio)\r\n\r\n==\u003e wayfinder/tickets/ticket-004.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 004: Bidirectional Visual Canvas Synchronization and Active Subgraph Illumination Specification\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-004.md`  \r\n**Scope:** GraphRAG Stage 4 - Canvas-Agent Interaction Bus  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-graphrag-spec`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-002.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow must the visual React canvas interact with the GraphRAG pipeline so that user actions on the graph seed conversational inquiries, and the exact subgraphs retrieved by GraphRAG illuminate on the canvas within $\u003c500\\text{ms}$?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Decision and Specification Requirements\r\n\r\n### 2.1. Canvas-to-Agent Event Flow\r\n1. **Interactive Node Click Handlers:**\r\n   - Selecting a node (e.g., `JURIS-DME-B (CGS)` or `CMS-MCD-A59508`) highlights the node on the canvas and populates a context card.\r\n   - Quick-action buttons trigger automated GraphRAG inquiries:\r\n     - *\"What states does this contractor cover?\"*\r\n     - *\"What diagnoses are approved under this coverage policy?\"*\r\n     - *\"What are the payment rates in my state?\"*\r\n2. **Context Seeding:**\r\n\r\n==\u003e wayfinder/tickets/ticket-005.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 005: Master Specification Synthesis and Edits for functional_specification_004.md\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-005.md`  \r\n**Scope:** Specification Compilation \u0026 Synthesis  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-graphrag-spec`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-001.md`, `ticket-002.md`, `ticket-003.md`, `ticket-004.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow must `functional_specification_004.md` be edited to completely replace the obsolete tool-calling/text-to-cypher model with the comprehensive, zero-hallucination GraphRAG specification defined across Tickets 001 through 004?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Decision and Specification Requirements\r\n\r\n### 2.1. Exact Sections in `functional_specification_004.md` Targeted for Edits\r\n\r\n1. **Document Title \u0026 Scope (Section 1):**\r\n   - Retitle to: `# Functional Specification: Browser-Based React Graph Visualization \u0026 Hugging Face GraphRAG Architecture`\r\n   - Explicitly define the three coupled pillars:\r\n     1. Interactive Graph Visualization\r\n     2. Hugging Face GraphRAG Engine (Zero bespoke queries, zero Cypher hallucination)\r\n     3. Bidirectional Canvas-Agent Synchronization\r\n"}}}
